                <pb facs="0584" n="500" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg500"/>

                <head>No. 246.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Steele to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gloucester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 5, 1886</date>.
                        [Received June 7.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose the master of the schooner Alice
                    M. Jordan’s affidavit for your consideration.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. STEELE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">President American Fishery
                            Union.</hi></signed></closer>




